index 38da080..7fa7f4d 100644
--- a/guild-idler-status.md
+++ b/guild-idler-status.md
@@ -22662,3 +22662,36 @@ Dev Update | Patch 0286
 **Raids list ordering**, unrelated bug found in the same screenshot set: `RaidsPanel`'s raid list renders `RAIDS` straight from `raids.json`'s own array order, which was never level-ordered (`requiem_last_god`, reqLevel 55, sat at index 2, ahead of four lower-level raids). `LorePanel`'s own "completed raids" list already explicitly re-sorts by `reqLevel` (`RAIDS.filter(...).sort((a, b) => a.reqLevel - b.reqLevel)`), confirming reqLevel is already the intended canonical order elsewhere in the codebase -- `RaidsPanel` was just never updated to match. Fixed by reordering `raids.json` itself (ascending `reqLevel`) rather than sorting at render time, so every consumer of `RAIDS` gets the same order for free without a scattered `.sort()` at each call site. Checked for any behavior that depends on array position before reordering: `isRaidUnlocked` treats `RAIDS.findIndex(...) === 0` as "always unlocked" (the guild's starter raid) -- `blackford_keep` (reqLevel 8) was already the lowest-level raid in the set, so it lands at index 0 again after the sort and this special case is unaffected. Every other unlock gate (`unlocksRaidId`, `requiresChainId`) is looked up by id, not index, so reordering the array has zero effect on any raid's actual unlock logic -- confirmed by reading `RAID_BY_ID`/`isRaidUnlocked`/`raidLockReason` and the full `unlocksRaidId` graph (`blackford_keep` -> `frozen_wyrmkeep` -> `bonewrought_vault`, everything else ungated by a prior raid) before making the change.
 
 **Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- no `GameState` shape changed; `chainOffer`'s stored `reqLevel` and `rewardGold`/`rewardXp` are byte-identical to before, only the runtime `previewSuccess` calculation and the static `raids.json` array order changed. Worth a real playtest confirming an out-leveled hero's chain-stage odds now track their board-contract odds at the same difficulty, and that the Raids tab now lists Blackford Keep through Requiem for the Last God in ascending level order.
+
+
+### Starter-experience polish: guaranteed tutorial win, clearer Guild Hall/facility text, whole-number Gear Score, hero renaming (patch 0287)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Patch 0287
+- Fixed: the very first quest can no longer come back a loss -- it's a guaranteed win behind the scenes, no matter what percentage the card shows
+- Changed: the Guild Hall's gold storage plaque now reads "Gold Storage Cap" and shows your current gold against it, instead of a bare number that looked like a starting balance
+- Changed: the Infirmary/Kennel facility line now reads "Auto heal time decreased by X minutes per level" instead of the cryptic "-X min heal time per level"
+- Fixed: a hero's Gear Score badge could show a long decimal (e.g. 29.2123213) instead of a whole number
+- Added: a free "Reroll Name" button on every hero card, picking a new name from their class's own name pool
+- Added: 5 new names to every hero class's name pool (5 -> 10 each), cutting down on same-class name collisions
+```
+
+**Reported directly**, alongside a screenshot of the Guild Hall: the gold storage plaque, the Infirmary/Kennel wording, and (from the Heroes list) two visibly duplicate names on the same roster ("Sir Corwin" at both Lv 22 and Lv 23, two "Dame Orla"s) prompting the rename + name-pool asks. Separately: the first quest's duration and success chance, and Gear Score/HP decimal display.
+
+**Tutorial quest duration -- already correct, no change needed.** `tutorialQuestOffer` (quests.ts) already sets `duration: 5 * MINUTE`. Confirmed by reading the function directly rather than assuming; nothing to fix here.
+
+**Tutorial quest success -- now actually guaranteed, not just high.** `tutorialQuestOffer` sets a high `baseSuccess: 90` specifically so the card reads like a genuine first success rather than a coin flip, per its own doc comment -- but the roll itself was still a real `rng.chance(finalSuccess)`, so a new player could still see their very first quest come back a failure on bad luck (or with `events.successDelta` pulling the roll down further). `QuestManager.resolve` already forces the injury/broken-gear branch for this exact quest id regardless of RNG (`isTutorialQuest || rng.chance(injuryRisk)`, patch predates this one) -- the success roll never got the same treatment. Fixed by hoisting `isTutorialQuest` above the `finalSuccess`/`success` calculation and short-circuiting it the identical way: `const success = isTutorialQuest || rng.chance(finalSuccess);`. The displayed percentage on the quest card is untouched (still whatever `previewSuccess` honestly computes) -- only the actual, hidden outcome is forced, matching the existing forced-injury convention exactly, including not consuming an rng draw when short-circuited (same as the pre-existing injury check already did).
+
+**Gold Storage plaque.** `GuildPanel.tsx`'s plaque showed only `formatGold(ModifierManager.goldStorage(state))` under the label "Gold Storage" -- a bare cap number with nothing marking it as a cap, easily read as "the guild starts with this much gold." The topbar's own gold readout (`MenuWindow.tsx`) already shows the identical number as `current / cap` (the "24.4k / 90.0k" format), so this plaque now matches that established convention: label reworded to "Gold Storage Cap", value shown as `{state.gold} / {storage cap}`.
+
+**Infirmary/Kennel wording.** `GuildPanel.tsx`'s facility card builder rendered `def.healTimeReductionMinutesPerLevel` as `-X min heal time per level` -- terse enough to read as "X minutes off something," not obviously the auto-heal timer. Reworded to `Auto heal time decreased by X minutes per level`, matching the plain-verb phrasing every other stat line in that same list already uses (`+X storage per level`, `+1 free Treat per day, per level`, etc.). Text-only change; `def.healTimeReductionMinutesPerLevel`'s value and the Infirmary/Kennel mechanics themselves are untouched.
+
+**Gear Score decimal display.** `HeroManager.gearScoreForInstance` (equipment.ts) converts an item's rolled stats through a `/6` ratio and applies a `(1 + item.plus * 0.15)` multiplier -- the sum `HeroManager.gearScore(hero)` returns is essentially never a whole number. None of its three call sites (`EquipmentPanel.tsx`, `HeroesPanel.tsx` x2) rounded before handing it to `GearScoreBadge`, so the badge, its title tooltip, and its progress-bar tooltip could all show a long float. Fixed once, inside `GearScoreBadge` itself, rather than at each call site: a `displayScore = Math.round(score)` used for every number actually shown to the player, while `tier`/`nextTier`/`progress` (and the tier-crossing flash) still key off the exact raw `score` so the progress bar and flash timing stay precise -- only the displayed digits changed.
+
+**HP decimal display -- checked, already correct, no bug found.** Both places a hero's or pet's Health is shown as a number (`HeroesPanel.tsx`'s `HealthBar`, `HatcheryPanel.tsx`'s pet equivalent) already wrap the current value in `Math.round(...)`, and `HeroManager.maxHealth`/`PetManager.maxHealth` both already `Math.round` their own return value -- so `Health 142/151` was already whole on both sides at both call sites. Read through every other HP-related render in `src/ui` (corner companion, raid party sprites) and found no numeric HP text there at all, only bar fills. Nothing changed here; noting it as explicitly checked rather than silently skipped, since it was reported alongside Gear Score as if both had the same bug.
+
+**Hero rename.** New `HeroManager.rerollName(hero, rng)`: picks a new name from `HERO_CLASSES[hero.heroClass].names` -- the same pool `create()` already draws from at recruitment -- excluding the hero's own current name whenever the pool has more than one option left, so a reroll always visibly changes something instead of occasionally landing back on the same name. `GameEngine.rerollHeroName(heroId)` wraps it (fresh seeded rng, notify, save), the same free/no-confirmation shape as the existing cosmetic skin picker (`setHeroSkin`) -- nothing is lost by rerolling, so no confirm dialog. New "⟲ Reroll Name" chip added to each hero's expanded card in `HeroesPanel.tsx`, next to the existing "Show on desktop" chip.
+
+**Hero name pool expansion.** Every one of the 13 classes in `hero-classes.json` had exactly 5 names -- confirmed directly from the data, and the reported Sir Corwin/Dame Orla collisions are exactly what a 5-name pool produces once a guild recruits more than a couple of heroes of the same class. Added 5 new, class-appropriate names to every class's own pool (5 -> 10 each: e.g. knight gains Sir Aldric/Dame Isolde/Sir Rowan/Dame Elowen/Sir Gavric; dwarf gains Borin/Freya Ironbrow/Dagna/Torvik/Old Hilde; full list in the diff), checked for no duplicate within any one class's own array before writing. Existing hero names on any current save are untouched -- this only widens the pool new recruits and rerolls draw from.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- no `GameState`/`Hero` shape changed; `rerollName` only ever writes a string already valid at hero creation into the same `hero.name` field. Worth a real playtest: send a fresh guild's starter hero on their first quest a few times (seed-dependent, so confirm across a couple of saves) to see it never fail, and try Reroll Name a few times on a hero to confirm it never silently repeats the same name back-to-back.
